{"status":"Error","code":"PermissionDenied","error":"Table 10076836 (Inventory Setup ori) cannot be written via Data.Records.Set. This is an internal table.","parameter":"tableNumber","received":"10076836","expected":"a table the user may write through the generic data types","nextStep":"Choose a table the user may access through the generic data types. This restriction cannot be bypassed by the request.","hint":"For usage details, call the \"Help.Implementation.Get\" message type with subject \"Data.Records.Set\". Always read the help before calling a message type."}

--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "strict": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "required": false,
      "default": false,
      "description": "Optional root Boolean, default false. Non-read types always refuse unknown data keys before execution with UnknownParameter; false does not opt out. Read types warn unless strict is true. Do not place this option inside data."
    },
    "subject": {
      "use": "optional",
      "forms": [
        "table name",
        "table number"
      ],
      "description": "The table: its name (e.g. Customer), its number (e.g. 18) or Namespace.Name. A table key under data replaces subject."
    },
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "dataRequired": true
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.tableName, data.tableNumber, data.tableNo, data.tableId",
      "form": "table name or number",
      "description": "The table name or number. The first key present is used and replaces subject: tableName, then tableNumber, tableNo, tableId."
    },
    {
      "source": "subject",
      "form": "table name or number",
      "description": "The table name, number or Namespace.Name, when no table key is sent under data."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.data[].id",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The SystemId of the record to update, per entry. Found: it is updated (a primaryKey sent as well must match its key fields). Not found: an error, unless identityInsert is true, then a record is inserted with that SystemId."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.data[].primaryKey",
      "form": "object",
      "description": "The key fields of the record, per entry, used when there is no id: the record with that key is updated, or inserted when there is none. To insert a record whose key the table assigns itself (a number series or auto-increment), name the key field with an empty value, for example {\"No_\": \"\"}."
    },
    {
      "source": "(neither)",
      "form": "none",
      "description": "An entry with neither an id nor a primaryKey that names a key field of the table is refused with InvalidParameter and nothing is written, so a key lost on the way never inserts a record."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "tableName",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Table name, e.g. Customer. Or send the table as subject."
    },
    {
      "name": "tableNumber",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Table number, e.g. 18. Aliases: tableNo, tableId."
    },
    {
      "name": "data",
      "type": "array",
      "required": true,
      "description": "The records to insert or update, as objects with only the properties id, identityInsert, primaryKey and fields. Send an object whose data property is this array; a bare array as the payload is not accepted. At least one entry, and every entry must be an object.",
      "children": [
        {
          "name": "id",
          "type": "string",
          "required": false,
          "description": "SystemId (GUID) of the record to update. A value that is not a GUID is an error. See target for what happens when no record has it. Not the SystemId field of a fields object: system fields are never written."
        },
        {
          "name": "primaryKey",
          "type": "object",
          "required": false,
          "description": "The primary key fields by JSON key (rule in notes). An entry without id has to name at least one key field here. To let the table assign its own key (a number series or auto-increment), name the key field with an empty value (an empty string, or 0 for a number), for example {\"No_\": \"\"}. A null value is refused."
        },
        {
          "name": "fields",
          "type": "object",
          "required": false,
          "description": "The other fields by JSON key. Sales and purchase line fields use dependency order; other tables use JSON key order. Each field's OnValidate runs as it is set. Primary key fields sent here are ignored."
        },
        {
          "name": "identityInsert",
          "type": "boolean",
          "required": false,
          "description": "true: an id that matches no record inserts a new record with that SystemId. Omitted: false."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "force",
      "type": "boolean",
      "required": false,
      "description": "true: write fields the change log write guard would block (only when the guard mode is Via force), and the company configuration fields that are otherwise never written: the posting window of General Ledger Setup, Closed and Date Locked of Accounting Period, No. Series and No. Series Line, and the VAT Registration No. and Registration No. of Company Information (in every guard mode, for setting up a company). Also opens User Setup (91, including your own row), IC Partner (413), Business Unit (220), Job Queue Entry (472), Alternative Address (5201), Employee Relative (5205) and Confidential Information (5216) for writes. Their write guard is unchanged: force bypasses it only in Via force mode. IC Partner fields 100-108 and Business Unit fields 26-27 stay closed. All forced writes need the BIFROST Force ori permission set. Omitted: false."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success when at least one record was inserted or updated."
      },
      {
        "name": "insertedCount",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "Records inserted."
      },
      {
        "name": "modifiedCount",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "Records updated."
      },
      {
        "name": "result",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "Every written record as stored, in request order, in the form Data.Records.Get answers it (an option or enum value is its caption in the language of the call). fields holds only the fields the entry sent (all fields when it sent none); primary key fields are under primaryKey. Forced writes to Alternative Address (5201), Employee Relative (5205) and Confidential Information (5216) return only id (SystemId) and primaryKey; fields is omitted.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The SystemId of the record (GUID without braces)."
          },
          {
            "name": "primaryKey",
            "type": "object",
            "description": "The primary key fields of the record.",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "<field name>",
                "type": "mixed",
                "description": "One entry per primary key field (SystemId excluded), under the key rule in notes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "fields",
            "type": "object",
            "description": "The non-key fields of the record.",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "<field name>",
                "type": "mixed",
                "description": "One entry per other field, in the culture-invariant form of its type; notes lists the exceptions."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "warnings",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "Optional warnings: InvalidParameter with severity low when a primary key sent under fields is ignored; identify the record with id or primaryKey. FieldChangedByBC when another validation or the write changes a sent field after its own validation. Each entry has code, message, parameter (data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0) and nextStep. Status stays Success. The field-change warning excludes normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields."
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "error": "A table is required: send tableName or tableNumber.",
      "when": "No table key holds a value and the subject is blank. parameter is tableName.",
      "fix": "Send the table name or number as tableName or tableNumber; Help.Tables.Get lists the tables."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "error": "Table \"{value}\" was not found (from {tableName|tableNumber|tableNo|tableId|subject}).",
      "when": "A name or a number that is no table. parameter names the key used and received the value.",
      "fix": "Find the table with Help.Tables.Get."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "error": "A table key (tableName, tableNumber, tableNo or tableId) is an object or an array; parameter names the key, received the value and expected what the key takes.",
      "when": "A text or a number is read as the name or the number of the table. A null or an empty string counts as not sent, so the next key, or the subject, names the table.",
      "fix": "Send the table as a name or a number, or leave the key out and send the table as the subject."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The table is internal and cannot be written through Data.Records.Set. Or the table is closed by default (it holds personal data) and no Bifrost Field Access row of type None opens it for the caller; the error then says it is closed by default.",
      "fix": "Use the dedicated message type nextStep names, when there is one. For a table closed by default, nextStep says that an administrator can open it for your user with a Bifrost Field Access row of type None."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "A force-openable company setup table is written without force true or without the BIFROST Force ori permission set.",
      "fix": "Send force true with Data.Records.Set as a holder of BIFROST Force ori. Connection and credential fields remain closed."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "error": "Inserting a record into table {id} ({name}) was refused.",
      "when": "A feature app refused the insert before the record was written. This includes identityInsert and an insert by primary key, and it includes a table force has opened so one field of an existing row can be changed. parameter is data[n], counting from 0. expected is an update of an existing record. Nothing of the call is saved. Updating an existing record is not refused by this check, and a write-once field stays write-once. The nextStep mentions a forced write only when force was requested and granted.",
      "fix": "This table is closed for inserts. Update an existing record."
    },
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "error": "Missing required 'data' array in request.",
      "when": "data is missing or null; a bare array as the payload counts as missing. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send an object with a data array."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "data is not an array, or an entry of data is not an object; parameter names it, e.g. data[2]. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send data as an array of record objects."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "data is an empty array, so there is no record to insert or update. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send at least one record object."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "error": "Field {name} ({n}) in table {id} ({table}) cannot be written via Data.Records.Set. Use {hint}.",
      "when": "A field the entry sends is write-restricted and a dedicated message type exists for it or for the table; nextStep names it. parameter names the JSON field key, received is the value sent (not the field number), and field and table captions follow the caller language. Nothing is written.",
      "fix": "Use the type nextStep names."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "error": "Field {name} ({number}) in table {tableNo} ({tableName}) is write-once and already has a value; it cannot be changed via Data.Records.Set.",
      "when": "The request names a field a feature app declared write-once (OnAfterIsFieldWriteOnceForDataRecords) and the record already holds a value in it. A value is accepted only when the record is created, or while the field is still blank. This applies to every caller: no Field Access row (None, Bypass or other) and no event reopens it. Help.Fields.Get shows writeOnce per field. expected is a field that is still blank on the record. Nothing is written.",
      "fix": "Leave the field out of the request. To use another value, create a new record."
    },
    {
      "code": "BlockedByWriteGuard",
      "error": "Field \"{fields}\" in table {id} must be included in the change log write guard setup to be updated via Bifrost.",
      "when": "The write guard is Blocked, or Via force without a usable force, and a field an entry sends (also under primaryKey) is not covered by Change Log. parameter is data[n].{fields or primaryKey}.{key} of the first blocked field, expected is a field the change log write guard allows, and the answer adds blockedFields[] (fieldNo, fieldName, fieldCaption), guardMode and forceAvailable. nextStep names the Create type for line and journal line tables and the guard setup or force for every other table. Nothing is written.",
      "fix": "Cover the field in Change Log or add a guard exception; when forceAvailable is true resend with force true. For documents and journal lines use the Create type nextStep names."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "force is not true or false.",
      "fix": "Send true or false."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].fields.{jsonName}\" is not valid base64.",
      "when": "A BLOB field value cannot be decoded as base64. parameter names the field, received is the sent value, expected is base64 and nextStep is translated for the caller. All entries are checked before writing; nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Encode the BLOB content as base64 and resend the value."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n]\" names no record: it has neither an id nor a primaryKey that names a key field of the table.",
      "when": "An entry has no id and its primaryKey is missing, empty, or names only fields that are not key fields; parameter is data[n], received is the entry as written and expected is an id or a primaryKey that names a key field of the table. An entry with another problem of its own (a property of the wrong type or a key that is no field) is not reported a second time. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send id, or primaryKey with the key fields. To let the table assign its own key, name the key field with an empty value, e.g. {\"No_\": \"\"}."
    },
    {
      "code": "UnknownParameter",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].{name}\" is not declared by this message type. Nothing was executed.",
      "when": "An entry has a property other than id, identityInsert, primaryKey or fields; parameter is data[n].{name}. Unknown keys are refused before handler validation or any write, even when strict is false.",
      "fix": "Remove the key or use the declared parameter suggested by nextStep."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].{property}\" has value \"{value}\", which is not {a GUID | true or false | object}.",
      "when": "id is not a GUID, identityInsert is not true or false, or primaryKey or fields is not an object; a null is none of them. Nothing of the call is saved; parameter, received and expected name the property.",
      "fix": "Send a GUID string for id, true or false for identityInsert and objects for primaryKey and fields."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].fields.{key}\" is null, which is not a value of its field.",
      "when": "A field or key field whose value is read is sent as a JSON null. Primary keys misplaced under fields are ignored with an InvalidParameter warning instead. A null for a field whose value is read does not clear it: it is refused, with parameter data[n].fields.{key} or data[n].primaryKey.{key}, received null and expected a value that is not null. To empty a field, send an empty string. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send the value in the form Data.Records.Get returns."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "error": "Invalid field \"{name}\" in {primaryKey or fields} object. Field does not exist in the target table.{Did you mean \"{suggestion}\"? Valid field names: ...}",
      "when": "A key is not a writable field of the table: it is misspelt, a FlowField, an obsolete field or a field the caller may not write. Every such key of every entry is listed; parameter is data[n].{fields or primaryKey}.{key}. Nothing of the call is saved. A system field is not an error: it is read-only, accepted and ignored.",
      "fix": "Use the keys Data.Records.Get returns; use the suggestion verbatim."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].fields.{key}\" has value \"{value}\", which cannot be read as a {date | time | date-time | decimal | 32-bit integer | 64-bit integer | boolean | GUID | duration | record id | date formula}, or is longer than the field.",
      "when": "A value is not in the form its field takes, or a Text or Code value is longer than the field (it is refused, never cut). Every such value of every entry is listed with parameter, received and expected. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send the value in the form Data.Records.Get returns."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "error": "Parameter \"data[n].fields.{key}\" has value \"{value}\", which is none of the names, captions or ordinals of the field. Valid values are: {list}",
      "when": "An option or enum field is sent a value that is none of its names, captions or ordinals. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Use a value from the list in the answer."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "error": "Record with SystemId {guid} not found. Use \"identityInsert\": true to insert a new record with this SystemId.",
      "when": "An entry has an id that matches no record and identityInsert is not true; parameter is data[n].id. This is found while the entries are written, one at a time. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Check the id, or send identityInsert true to insert with that SystemId."
    },
    {
      "code": "ConflictingIdentifiers",
      "error": "Primary key does not match the record with SystemId {guid}",
      "when": "An entry sends both id and primaryKey and the key fields differ from the record's; parameter is data[n].primaryKey. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Send the matching key, or leave primaryKey out."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "error": "{Document Type} {No.} is in pending approval and requested changes are not allowed.",
      "when": "A Released sales or purchase line would change a commercial field, even with an unchanged amount; reopen the document first. A sales or purchase header or line that is Released or Pending Approval would change its Amount Including VAT or its bill-to / pay-to; parameter is data[n] counting from 0 (the first entry is data[0]), expected is a change that leaves the amount and the customer or vendor as they are. This is found while the entries are written, one at a time. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Reopen the document first (cancel the approval request), or leave those fields alone."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "error": "Error processing record {n}",
      "when": "Business Central answered the insert of an entry with false instead of an error, because a record with that primary key already exists. The message counts from 1 (the first entry is \"Error processing record 1\") and parameter counts from 0 (the first entry is data[0]). expected is a primary key that no other record of the table has. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Check with Data.Records.Get whether the record exists already, then send the call again."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "error": "Error processing record {n}",
      "when": "Business Central answered the modify of an entry with false instead of an error, because the record is gone. The message counts from 1 (the first entry is \"Error processing record 1\") and parameter counts from 0 (the first entry is data[0]). expected is a record that still exists. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Check with Data.Records.Get that the record still exists, then send the call again."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "Business Central's own error text",
      "when": "Business Central refuses the operation, e.g. a value that fails the field's validation, a key that is not unique in a table a trigger writes, or no write permission on the table. A known field validation names data[n].fields.<jsonName> with localized expected and nextStep; a record-level failure names data[n] without guessing a field. Nothing of the call is saved.",
      "fix": "Read the text: it names the field or setup to fix."
    },
    {
      "code": "MultipleErrors",
      "when": "More than one request value is wrong (force, data, then each entry of data in order: its properties, then the keys and values of primaryKey and fields); errors[] lists each in this order.",
      "fix": "Fix every listed value. Nothing was read."
    },
    {
      "code": "Retryable",
      "when": "A transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. The error preserves Business Central's original text. Uncaught queue-path errors remain BusinessCentralError.",
      "fix": "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "write",
    "changes": "Inserts or updates the records in data and runs the validation of each field sent. All or nothing: everything that can be checked without writing is checked first, and one failing entry rolls the whole call back. Ledger entries and posted document headers are saved through Business Central's own edit routines.",
    "idempotent": false,
    "preconditions": [
      "The table is not an internal table and the caller may write it.",
      "Every field sent is a writable field of the table and the change log write guard lets it through (Open mode, Change Log coverage, a guard exception, or force in Via force mode)."
    ]
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Data.Records.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You need a template record: it returns the same shape and the exact keys."
    },
    {
      "name": "Data.Notes.Set",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You want to add or change notes, not field values."
    },
    {
      "name": "Help.Fields.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You need the fields of the table, their types and their write restrictions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Help.Tables.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You need to know whether a table is writable."
    },
    {
      "name": "Purchase.Document.Create",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You are writing purchase documents with lines: the write guard blocks Purchase Line here."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sales.Document.Create",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You are writing sales documents with lines: the write guard blocks Sales Line here."
    },
    {
      "name": "Finance.GeneralJournal.Create",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You are writing general journal lines: use it instead of Gen. Journal Line here."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.ItemJournal.Create",
      "useInsteadWhen": "You are writing item journal lines: use it instead of Item Journal Line here."
    }
  ],
  "workflow": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "messageType": "Help.Tables.Get",
        "purpose": "Confirm the table is writable and get its number."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Help.Fields.Get",
        "purpose": "List its fields: numbers, types, options and write restrictions."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Data.Records.Get",
        "purpose": "Read one record with take 1 as a template with the exact keys."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Data.Records.Set",
        "purpose": "Edit fields in the template and send it back."
      }
    ],
    "text": "Do this for a table you have not written before."
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Insert a customer with its own number",
      "request": {
        "type": "Data.Records.Set",
        "subject": "Customer",
        "data": {
          "data": [
            {
              "primaryKey": {
                "No_": "XTEST-12345"
              },
              "fields": {
                "Name": "Test Customer",
                "City": "Reykjavik"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "insertedCount": 1,
        "modifiedCount": 0,
        "result": [
          {
            "id": "<systemId>",
            "primaryKey": {
              "No_": "XTEST-12345"
            },
            "fields": {
              "Name": "Test Customer",
              "City": "Reykjavik"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Update one field of a record found by SystemId",
      "request": {
        "type": "Data.Records.Set",
        "subject": "Customer",
        "data": {
          "data": [
            {
              "id": "<systemId>",
              "fields": {
                "City": "Akureyri"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "insertedCount": 0,
        "modifiedCount": 1,
        "result": [
          {
            "id": "<systemId>",
            "primaryKey": {
              "No_": "XTEST-12345"
            },
            "fields": {
              "City": "Akureyri"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Inserts or updates records of any writable Business Central table from JSON in the Data Shipping shape (id, primaryKey, fields), the shape Data.Records.Get returns. The whole call is one transaction. Writes to fields are guarded by the change log write guard.",
  "notes": "Keys: The JSON key of a table field is its field name with the characters % . \" \\ / and the apostrophe turned into an underscore and every other character that is not a letter or digit removed: No. becomes No_, Sell-to Customer No. becomes SelltoCustomerNo_, Balance (LCY) becomes BalanceLCY. Use the keys exactly as Data.Records.Get returns them. Order: primary key fields are set first. Sales Line and Purchase Line fields use dependency order, whatever the order of the JSON keys: Type, No., Variant Code, Location Code, Unit of Measure Code, Quantity, Unit Price or Direct Unit Cost, Line Discount %, Line Discount Amount, then remaining fields in request order. Other tables validate fields in request order; send a controlling field before its dependent field. Malformed BLOB, Media and MediaSet content is refused with InvalidParameterFormat before any row is written; parameter identifies data[n].fields.<jsonName>, with expected and localized nextStep. Values: dates YYYY-MM-DD, date-times ISO 8601, decimals with a dot, booleans true or false, GUIDs with or without braces; an option or enum by name, caption or ordinal; BLOB as Base64; Media as Base64 or {Value: Base64}; MediaSet as Base64, {Value: Base64}, or {Media: [{Value: Base64}]}; a currency field equal to the LCY code is stored blank; a Dimension Set ID by number or as an array of {DimensionCode, DimensionValueCode}. A value that cannot be read as the field's date, time, date-time, decimal, integer, boolean, GUID, duration, record id or date formula is refused with InvalidParameterFormat, naming the entry and the field (data[1].fields.Amount), and so is a Text or Code value longer than the field (it is never cut); nothing of the call is saved, so a Success always means every value was written. An Integer field takes a 32-bit whole number and a BigInteger field a 64-bit one. Everything in the request that can be checked without writing is checked first, for every entry, and every problem is reported to